  "scope": "Standard two-tier cumulative loss dominance is equivalent to unanimity within an explicitly defined family of additive diagnostics with positive natural base and severity increment. The strict version, crossed-case reversal, invariance under repeated ground reports, raw-row counting failure, and a common-support dependency counterexample are checked. Equal direct profiles need not determine shared continuation; the inherited J comparator distinguishes that omitted dependency. Actual unit individuation, tier classification, completeness, normative LC force, permissions and appropriate chances are substantive premises. No additive ethical utility, decisive choice, empirical calibration or universal ordering is established.",
